\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0 For my homestead and its quiet
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj Longs my weary heart again.
\par There awaits me joy in fullness,
\par Purest pleasure without pain.
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj For my homestead and its quiet
\par Longs my hopeful heart again,
\par My hopeful heart, my hopeful heart
\par For my homestead, for my homestead.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. In my homestead peace is dwelling,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 Peace the earth holds not in store.
\par Which with pure and sacred voices,
\par Even seraphs all adore.
\par For my homestead and its quiet....
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  In my homestead joy is dwelling,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 Such as mortals cannot know.
\par There the soul is free from suff'ring,
\par Knows no earthly pain or woe.
\par For my homestead and its quiet....
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  T'wards my homestead I am travelling,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 Once afar, yet now so near,
\par Where hope's golden stars are shining,
\par O'er that heavenly blessed sphere.
\par For my homestead and its quiet...\i\f1\fs14 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\i0\f2\fs14 
\par }

